      "translations": {
        "en": "Indeed, Ali (peace be upon him) was among you, so he went to the Banu Diwan and bought three garments for one Dinar: the shirt up to above the ankle, the lower garment up to half the calf, and the cloak from his front up to his chest and from his back up to his lower back. Then he raised his hand to the sky and did not cease to praise Allah for what He had clothed him with until he entered his house. Then he said: 'This is the clothing that is befitting for the Muslims to wear.'"
      }
